Create your own future

Create your own future

Connect critical systems within one of the bank’s most complex business domains. Develop solutions while learning how securities processes work from end to end. Use innovation and AI to help us improve and work smarter.

That is what you will use your talents for as a Junior Developer Securities Systems Integration at Van Lanschot Kempen. You develop interfaces and features that connect systems, markets and data sources across the securities domain. Together with your colleagues, you take responsibility for both running and changing the application landscape. You receive support from experienced team members while gradually building your technical knowledge, business understanding and ownership.

You also have the following tasks:

developing interfaces and features within the securities domain;
translating business needs into clear and maintainable technical solutions;
taking shared responsibility for both the continuity and development of the team’s solutions;
contributing to the modernisation of our technology landscape;
exploring how AI can improve quality, accelerate development and help the team work smarter.

Your talents

Curious, entrepreneurial and eager to learn. This is how we can best describe you in the position of Junior Developer Securities Systems Integration. Talents that you use to guide our customers in a constantly changing world every day. By thinking out of the box and asking questions.

You enjoy taking ownership and are not afraid to explore a complex business domain. You want to understand not only how a solution works technically, but also why the solution matters within the securities process.

a bachelor’s or master’s degree in software engineering, computer science or a related field, or equivalent experience;
experience with C#, .NET, Azure and integration technologies;
an interest in DevOps, run-and-change responsibility and complex business processes;
the ability to make practical use of AI tools and explore how these tools can improve your work;
good mastery of English, both oral and written.

Move ahead at Van Lanschot Kempen

Investing in line with our clients' beliefs and goals, supporting them in future-oriented, sustainable and data-driven decision-making. Both nationally and internationally. With nearly 300 years of experience, we make this ambition a reality at Van Lanschot Kempen. We do this with some 2,300 colleagues in various fields of expertise.

The Securities Systems Integration team connects systems, markets and data sources across the securities domain. Our interfaces support securities processes such as ordering, trading, settlement and reporting. The team is jointly responsible for run and change. We combine continuity with modernisation and create room for innovation, technical improvement and the practical use of AI.

An organisation's degree of innovation and agility also depends on the diversity of its workforce. Our differences make us stronger together. We promote an inclusive work environment where all colleagues feel at home. With us, you can be yourself. And we are proud of that.

Curious about the stories of colleagues and how they experience working at Van Lanschot Kempen? Go to People & Projects and find out more! Or listen to our Podcast series to hear what our colleagues have to say.

Turning talent into value!

That's what we do! The fact is, if you add value, you can expect the same from us in return. A good work-life balance with our hybrid way of working is a good example of this. As a Junior Developer Securities Systems Integration, you will also be given:

A competitive salary according to your experience. 
Training and development opportunities within software engineering and the securities domain;
Guidance from experienced colleagues while taking increasing ownership;
Flexible working hours and hybrid working arrangements;
Access to professional communities and events across Van Lanschot Kempen.

And we have many other employment benefits ready for you. Discover all the benefits of working at Van Lanschot Kempen.

